      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While Marcus's hoodie and Andre's police history provide immediate visual cues, these specific choices do risk reinforcing racialized tropes by implicitly tying his clothing to \"the streets\" and his background to criminality. To avoid this, consider adding nuanced details that complicate those instant assumptions, such as why Marcus pays rent elsewhere or why Andre holds a specific, licensed job. Ultimately, these descriptions work well as starting points, but ensuring Marcus engages with the narrative beyond just his perceived identity will help prevent them from feeling like standard archetypes.",
