      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no rule that certain races \"fit\" genres better based on race itself; rather, this often stems from historical storytelling patterns and Hollywood conventions rather than any inherent truth about the characters. Audiences might expect diversity in different genres because major studios have historically underrepresented actors from marginalized groups in these specific roles, creating a feedback loop of perception. Writing requires intentional deconstruction of these expectations so that the character's strength comes from their unique personality rather than their demographic, allowing you to tell one of these dramas authentically regardless of the cast.",
